<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Which tags Ottomatic offers to handle.

  The matching rule is worth knowing before editing this: within one <tech-list>
  the tag must support *every* tech listed (AND), between lists any one group is
  enough (OR), and there is **no negation**. So IsoDep — what a bank card or a
  transit card speaks — cannot be excluded directly. The way to leave those alone
  is to name techs they do not have:

    NTAG21x sticker    [NfcA, MifareUltralight, Ndef]          matches
    blank NTAG         [NfcA, MifareUltralight, NdefFormatable] matches
    EMV payment card   [IsoDep, NfcA]                           matches nothing

  Never list bare NfcA/NfcB/IsoDep here: each of those would catch every payment
  card on the phone, and Ottomatic would start appearing in the tag-handling
  chooser every time somebody taps their wallet.

  Ndef and NdefFormatable never co-exist on one tag — a tag is either formatted or
  it is not — so both groups are needed to cover written and blank stickers.
  MifareClassic is left out on purpose: it would pick up Classic stickers, but it
  would also pick up a great many transit cards.
-->
<resources>
    <tech-list>
        <tech>android.nfc.tech.Ndef</tech>
    </tech-list>
    <tech-list>
        <tech>android.nfc.tech.NdefFormatable</tech>
    </tech-list>
    <tech-list>
        <tech>android.nfc.tech.MifareUltralight</tech>
    </tech-list>
    <tech-list>
        <tech>android.nfc.tech.NfcV</tech>
    </tech-list>
</resources>
